                <pb facs="0247" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Torreon</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Donaldson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Torreon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-05T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 6—2:12
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Chinese Chamber of Commerce have requested me to represent Chinese people in case
                    of emergency. Awaiting instructions.</p>
                <p>No change in the situation hereabouts. The Government has withdrawn all of the
                    military forces from Durango and sent them to Mexico City.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Donald</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >son</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
